baseline:
Information Security and Cybersecurity. The Counterparty shall implement and maintain administrative, technical, physical and organisational security measures appropriate to the nature, sensitivity and risk of the Personal Data, data and systems involved in the Services, including:
(a) access controls, multi-factor authentication and least-privilege principles;
(b) encryption of Personal Data and sensitive information in transit and at rest;
(c) logging, monitoring and anomaly detection;
(d) vulnerability management and timely patching; and
(e) incident-response and forensic-investigation capabilities.
The Counterparty shall maintain its security measures to at least the standards required by Applicable Law and shall not degrade them without the Company's approval.

buyside:
